# Installed to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile on the box; `sudo systemctl reload caddy`.
#
# Caddy obtains and renews a Let's Encrypt certificate per hostname
# automatically. Certificates are managed independently, so a hostname whose DNS
# is not yet pointed here fails only its own challenge and is retried with
# backoff — it cannot stop the others from serving.

# Shared behaviour. Caddy sets X-Forwarded-For, which server/index.js reads via
# `trust proxy: 1`, so the per-IP demo limits see real visitor addresses rather
# than 127.0.0.1. /api/health echoes clientIp specifically so a deploy can prove
# this still works.
#
# WebSocket upgrades for /api/voice/stream need no special configuration —
# reverse_proxy passes them through natively.
(app) {
	encode gzip zstd
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000
}

# All three registered domains serve the same site.
#
# NOTE: this is not canonicalised. Identical content on three domains splits SEO
# authority and lets search engines index whichever they prefer. Once there is a
# decision on the primary domain, the other two apexes should 301 to it the same
# way the www hosts below do. Serving all three is the correct interim state —
# every domain a visitor might try resolves and works.
audeora.in, audeora.ai, audeora.com {
	import app
}

# One canonical hostname per domain: www redirects rather than serving a
# duplicate, so links, analytics and search results converge on a single URL.
www.audeora.in {
	redir https://audeora.in{uri} permanent
}

www.audeora.ai {
	redir https://audeora.ai{uri} permanent
}

www.audeora.com {
	redir https://audeora.com{uri} permanent
}

# Fallback hostname, kept deliberately.
#
# nip.io resolves <dashed-ip>.nip.io to that IP, giving Caddy a real hostname to
# certify without a domain. It stays so there is always a working HTTPS URL if a
# domain's DNS is mid-change or misconfigured, and so a deploy can be verified
# before propagation.
#
# The address is the Elastic IP 18.60.197.184 and so is stable across stop/start.
# If the instance's address ever changes, this line must be updated to match or
# its certificate will stop validating.
18-60-197-184.nip.io {
	import app
}
